		{"id":"779b351a300a57de","x":-341,"y":-281,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"[[Timora Fayerine.canvas]]\n#PlayerCharacter "},
		{"id":"05b42594260320eb","x":-341,"y":-160,"width":865,"height":530,"type":"text","text":"Born a noble child in the city of Dásos Neroú a city located between the Milorian coast and the city of Volstar, Timora’s childhood was full of fun and colourful faces from all of the foot traffic in and out of the city. Her family is of a noble status and both her brother and sister act like the nobles they were programmed by culture to be. Timora never cared for her nobility and often pulled pranks for the attention it would get from her mother Vilura. Vilura was an avid follower of Milora and so is the rest of the Fayerine family. Timora always had a knack and gift for both the art of performing and using magic during her acts. In school she often ditched all of her classes to get one on one training in the ways of music and magic through the high principal Xynthrani, a drow woman who loved both music and children. Although she always had an eventful life whether through street performances or pulling pranks on those around her, there was always something missing, a curiosity that her mother was always against her pursuing. Timora never knew her father and anytime she asked her mother about it, her mother’s face would be shadowed with a sad complexion and she would always say to stop asking and that she does not know anything about him anymore. Eventually tragedy struck and Vilura fell ill to a rare disease known as arcania, an illness that strikes those who have an incredibly weak aptitude for magic. During one argument about Timora’s father Vilura passed away. Written in her will she left everything to Timora and so both siblings resented her for it blaming Timora for Vilura's death because of the magic she uses and also despising the fact that she got everything while they were left a small villa in the common area of the city. A few months later Timora left her home leaving her maid Sytha in charge of keeping the home and set off on a quest to spread her music, chaos and charm on the world, all in a pursuit to find her father to get the answers she's always seeked. Currently Timora just arrived at the city of Volstar and is staying in an inn called Alberts Ales where she has been earning money performing every night. She has been in Volstar for a few days now and is eager to see the rest of the world that awaits her."}
	],
